/**
 * Journey C — Revised work product (docs/END_TO_END_ACCEPTANCE.md).
 *
 * Real production build + real Chromium + the scripted provider; reuses the
 * journey-B finance flow (regenerated byte-identical CSV fixtures uploaded
 * through the real chat picker) and then turns the produced report into an
 * edited, rewritten, versioned, and exported document through the real
 * Documents workbench. Covers:
 *   - a real chat turn (query_data → render_chart → create_report) that
 *     persists a legacy report with the independently computed June numbers
 *     as its query table; the chat receipts (query result, chart card,
 *     report card) render in the real UI;
 *   - "Create editable copy" through the real ReportsView button → the copy's
 *     revision 1 deep-equals the stored legacy payload and is honestly
 *     unverified; the original report's HTML/PDF bytes are hash-verified
 *     unchanged across every later copy/edit/rewrite/publish step and the
 *     full backend restart;
 *   - a manual one-sentence correction with ZERO provider calls (asserted via
 *     the provider request counters), then a selected-passage rewrite driven
 *     by the scripted provider: inspect the diff, REJECT once, request again
 *     with a second scripted proposal, ACCEPT; unrelated sections, tables,
 *     and chart state stay byte-identical (stored-revision comparison +
 *     rendered workbench);
 *   - concurrency and CAS: a head move under an open UI draft surfaces the
 *     conflict dialog with the local draft preserved and the explicit
 *     reapply path lands a new revision; stale revision CAS saves are 409
 *     with current-head metadata; a stale proposal can never be accepted
 *     (409 + durable `stale`, inspectable-then-dismissible); a publish with a
 *     stale expected head is 409 `DOCUMENT_REVISION_CONFLICT` with
 *     current-head metadata (`DOCUMENT_HEAD_MOVED` is the completion-time
 *     recheck code) plus the UI recovery surface;
 *   - TWO published versions through the real publish button (immutable older
 *     exports hash-verified after the newer publish; v2 supersedes v1), one
 *     operation-UUID replay proves publication idempotency, and all four
 *     frozen-version exports are downloaded through real authenticated
 *     browser downloads: HTML self-contained (no external src/href, CSP,
 *     nosniff), PDF `%PDF-` magic + nontrivial bytes, the Markdown ZIP holds
 *     a real document.md + relative chart PNG assets + manifest.json with
 *     verified CRCs, and the DOCX is a readable OOXML zip whose
 *     word/document.xml carries the narrative and a native table;
 *   - rewrite bounds: the >8,000-char honest UI gate plus server 400
 *     OVERSIZE/INVALID (including a split surrogate pair), 409 selection-hash
 *     mismatch, and 409 one-active-rewrite;
 *   - foreign accounts get 404 on documents/publications/exports; a
 *     same-instance share recipient gets read-only detail with the payload
 *     omitted and is denied editable-copy;
 *   - closed dialogs keep their error/success slots (duplicate-template-name
 *     409 surfaces inside the dialog, closed dialog leaks nothing);
 *   - a full backend restart proves the durable document/revision/
 *     publication/rewrite history and frozen export bytes survive.
 *
 * Documented acceptance-harness capability gap (reported, not worked around):
 * the chat turn DOES render a chart (the chart card shows in chat), but a
 * scripted provider can never reference it inside the same turn's
 * `create_report` call: chart ids are server-minted run-scoped random UUIDs
 * and the fixture replays static step scripts (no tool-result echo), so the
 * 12-character model-garble fallback cannot match. The legacy report
 * therefore carries the query table + narrative with an EMPTY chart list,
 * and the chart-bearing document surfaces (chart PNGs in the Markdown ZIP /
 * DOCX, evidence appendix numbering, revision-bound charts) are exercised on
 * a second document created through the product's own first-party
 * explicit-tree creation contract (`POST /api/documents` `{tree}` — the same
 * service shape M16 composes) and published/exported through the real
 * workbench.
 *
 * Skipped sub-check with reason: "a legacy report with no stored payload".
 * Product code only ever creates reports through a completed agent turn, and
 * the normalized payload is dropped only when its serialization exceeds
 * 400,000 chars; with per-tool-call arguments bounded at 20,000 chars and the
 * provider script body bounded at 256 KiB, no scripted turn (and no
 * delete-payload API) can produce a payload-less report inside this harness.
 * The reachable honest boundary IS exercised: copies are owner-only (foreign
 * 404), and the recipient of a share never sees the payload nor may copy.
 *
 * Screenshots use the harness's content-free sequential names. Numeric
 * expectations come only from `fixtures/lib/finance-expected.mjs`.
 */
